\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Routing decision space showing the six test pairs positioned by their texture sparseness ($S$) and lighting difference ($D$) scores. Decision boundaries at $S=0.35$, $S=0.65$, $D=0.20$, and $D=0.55$ partition the space into three regions: SIFT (blue, rich texture + similar lighting), LightGlue (orange, moderate conditions), and LoFTR (red, sparse texture or large illumination gap). Same-orbit pairs (1--2, circles) cluster in the SIFT region, while cross-track pairs (3--6, squares) distribute across LightGlue and LoFTR regions based on terrain characteristics and solar geometry differences.}}{10}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:routing_space}{{4}{10}{Routing decision space showing the six test pairs positioned by their texture sparseness ($S$) and lighting difference ($D$) scores. Decision boundaries at $S=0.35$, $S=0.65$, $D=0.20$, and $D=0.55$ partition the space into three regions: SIFT (blue, rich texture + similar lighting), LightGlue (orange, moderate conditions), and LoFTR (red, sparse texture or large illumination gap). Same-orbit pairs (1--2, circles) cluster in the SIFT region, while cross-track pairs (3--6, squares) distribute across LightGlue and LoFTR regions based on terrain characteristics and solar geometry differences}{figure.4}{}}
